 because this has been just a  horrific year for so many because lives  have been lost  not to mention if it wasn't lives it was  livelihoods  so and then there's some people that you  know may not have been affected so  and everything in between so the tone i  think is is to be  um you know optimistic and hopeful but  reflective  the nypd will bar the general public  from congregating anywhere near times  square  the only people that will be there  besides the performers will be  about 40 people who are our invited  special guests  in years past the onstage production  featured special guests who joined the  mayor in pressing the waterford button  that triggers the ball drop  this year first responders frontline and  essential workers will be the ones  honored  but they'll remain in socially distant  seating areas with their families  rather than pressing the countdown  button  the audience will also include a small  group of guests who've rented for the  night this dome  on nasdaq's terrace overlooking times  square  airbnb which debuted on nasdaq earlier  in december  says the guests who signed up for this  marketing gimmick are paying 21  new york isn't alone in finding ways to  adapt new year's celebrations to the  pandemic  some cities are canceling them  altogether as americans start the day on  december 31st  sydney will kick off the new year with a  scaled-down version of its annual  fireworks display  hong kong is doing away entirely with  its fireworks display over victoria  harbor  officials say it's due to the pandemic  the government also canceled it last  year  citing the threat posed by  anti-government protesters  london now in lockdown has cancelled all  public events  including its fireworks show and las  vegas  which earlier launched an ad campaign to  let people know it's open again  won't hold its annual pyrotechnics  display on the strip  instead the city is promoting a virtual  event where it plans to blow up a 2020  sign  live at an undisclosed location  here in new york city where they've been  around twenty thousand deaths from covid  the organizers of the event say they  want the tone despite the pandemic  to be celebratory and hopeful  staring at the ball being a part of such  a rich american  iconic visual of this ball dropping  i feel like will really make people feel  like okay it's official now it's 20 21  and a sense of relief and a sense of  hope  and in a nod to the year that was  two-time grammy award winner gloria  gainer will sing the lyrics  go on now walk out that door just turn  around now  you're not welcome anymore which i think  is the way we all feel about 2020.  the message from public officials  worldwide you can help make  2021 a year to celebrate by spending new  year's  at home
 

